        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/sql-injection-identifier-injection",
          "ruleIndex": 14,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "SQL injection / identifier injection — Ruled out: Adjacent local SQLite datasources (skills_local_datasource.dart, chat_local_datasource.dart)\n\nSwept the sibling SQLite datasources for the same class. `skills_local_datasource.dart` and `chat_local_datasource.dart` use only `db.query/insert/delete` with `where: 'id = ?'` / `where: 'profile_id = ?'` + `whereArgs` (:117-167, :142-146, :146, :187, :210, :229). The only variable identifiers are compile-time constants `importedTableName = 'imported_skills'` and `statesTableName = 'skill_states'` (skills_local_datasource.dart:16-17) — not attacker-influenced, so no identifier injection. `CREATE TABLE`/`CREATE INDEX` statements are static strings. Chat history additionally goes to FlutterSecureStorage rather than SQLite (:119, :130)."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
