            "text": "Unvalidated URL scheme / intent smuggling via a Tier-2 launcher tool — Ruled out: open_external_url tool (tool_registry.dart:1420)\n\ncontact_launcher_tools.dart:155-180 openExternalUrl validates `uri.isScheme('http') || uri.isScheme('https')` AND `uri.host.isNotEmpty` before launching with LaunchMode.externalApplication — so `intent://`, `market://`, `javascript:`, `file://`, and `tel:` cannot be smuggled through model-supplied arguments. The Tier-2 `checkPermission` field is indeed absent at tool_registry.dart:1420, which is the enforcement-point defect owned by the Tier-2 Gate agent, but there is no unvalidated-scheme weakness here."
