          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/fts5-match-syntax-error-handling-availability-not-injection",
          "ruleIndex": 21,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "FTS5 MATCH syntax-error handling / availability (not injection) — No issue identified: _sanitizeFtsQuery keyword passthrough → FTS5 MATCH error path\n\nFTS5 keyword injection is not a security issue but IS an unhandled error. `_extractWords` keeps letters, so an uppercase `AND`/`OR`/`NOT` survives into `_sanitizeFtsQuery`, producing e.g. `buy* OR milk* OR AND* OR bread*`; FTS5 (keywords are case-sensitive) raises `fts5: syntax error near \"AND\"`. Empirically reproduced with real sqlite3 FTS5: `'buy milk AND bread'`, `'milk OR bread'`, `'NOT milk'`, `'this OR that'` all raise; lowercase `and`/`or` parse as terms. Impact is confined to availability of a local feature — no query alteration, no data exposure; the error string is `fts5: syntax error near \"X\"` and carries no rows. Note the two backends differ: sqlite_memory_datasource.dart:288-304 catches and falls back to `_searchWithLike`, while the LIVE implementation local_memory_service.dart:313-330 has no such catch, so the throw reaches :334 and returns `Left(StorageFailure('memory_unavailable'))`; agent_cubit.dart:522-526 ignores the Left, leaving `_activeMemories` stale rather than cleared. Severity low/informational — carried in open_items rather than filed as a vulnerability."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "_sanitizeFtsQuery keyword passthrough → FTS5 MATCH error path"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "strix": {
              "coverage_outcome": "no_issue_found",
              "risk_area": "FTS5 MATCH syntax-error handling / availability (not injection)",
              "surface": "_sanitizeFtsQuery keyword passthrough → FTS5 MATCH error path",
              "recorded_by": "Memory Vault FTS5 Injection",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
