          "message": {
            "text": "Unauthorized sensitive-data collection / permission bypass — Ruled out: FlamesHealthConnect.kt + lib/data/datasources/tools/chat/health_service.dart (Health Connect reads)\n\nRead is gated in Dart code, not just the manifest: health_service.dart:195-203 resolves HealthMetrics.permissionByMetric[metric] and rejects with 'health_permission_denied' unless grantedPermissions.contains(permission), immediately before _platform.readMetric at :205. The native side re-checks: FlamesHealthConnect.kt:75 returns null when permissionFor(metric) is null and Health Connect's own permissionController enforces the grant (health_service.dart:196-203 reads grantedPermissions from it). Tool is tier2Permission with checkPermission: () => service.checkPermission() (tool_registry.dart:1704-1705), and checkPermission (health_service.dart:243-260) returns false unless a supported metric's permission is actually granted. No health data is read by default or pushed continuously; the read is explicit-call-only. Data goes to the user's configured LLM as a tool result like any other tool. No hardcoded alternate endpoint."
