            "text": "Unauthorized sensitive-data collection and exfiltration to an unexpected endpoint — No issue identified: Device sensor tools: location, camera (built-in + external UVC), contacts, NFC, clipboard\n\nLocation: tool is tier2Permission with checkPermission: () => locationService.checkPermission() (tool_registry.dart:317). location_service.dart:26-34 checks isLocationServiceEnabled() then geolocator.checkPermission() and returns false unless whileInUse/always; getLocation re-checks at :62-75 before any position read. Camera: camera_take_photo is tier2Permission (tool_registry.dart:372); external_camera_capture is tier2Permission with checkPermission: () => service.isCameraPermissionGranted() (tool_registry.dart:446) and its own USB-permission check (tool_registry.dart:474-497). Frames/preview are rendered to a Flutter texture (external_camera_preview_cubit.dart:118-162) — no network code exists in external_camera_service.dart (grep for http/url/socket/upload returns nothing); a captured frame only leaves the device when the model receives it as a tool result from the user's own configured LLM. Contacts: checkPermission at tool_registry.dart:1366. NFC: nfc_read_tag and nfc_read_emoney_balance are tier2Permission (tool_registry.dart:1568, 1621) with device NFC-enabled checks. Clipboard: clipboard_read/clipboard_write are tier1Auto (tool_registry.dart:273, 291) — read of the user's own clipboard to the user's own configured server, no third party involved. No hardcoded or config-driven alternate endpoint exists for any of these: the only outbound destinations in the app are the user-configured LLM base URL and gateway URL."
