            "text": "Data egress to an unexpected/hardcoded third-party endpoint; sensitive data in logs — No issue identified: Outbound endpoint inventory + logging of sensitive values (whole app)\n\nExhaustive grep for analytics/telemetry/crash SDKs in pubspec.yaml, lib/ and android/app/build.gradle.kts found no Firebase, Crashlytics, Sentry, Amplitude or Mixpanel dependency. The only outbound destinations are: (1) the user-configured LLM base URL (agent_cubit.dart:121 default 'https://api.openai.com/v1', overridable per server profile), (2) the user-configured Hermes gateway URL (gateway_client.dart:149-151 scheme handling), (3) hardcoded GitHub release URLs for Piper TTS voice models (lib/domain/entities/chat/piper_voice.dart:37,48,59), and (4) a wa.me deep link built for the user to tap (contact_launcher_tools.dart:128-130). Device data (health/location/screen/camera/notifications) is never sent to (3) or (4). Note the local_memory_service.dart:282,335,474 developer.log calls emit only the string 'memory_unavailable' plus a truncated DB error reason — no memory content, no key, no secret. No log/print/debug path emits an API key, bearer token, or Authorization header."
