          "message": {
            "text": "Tool tier downgrade from remote/untrusted input (HITL bypass) — Ruled out: ToolRegistry tier gate (SecurityTier enforcement) vs remote skill/gateway/model input\n\nTier gating is decided purely by local constants: securityTier is set literally at each RegisteredTool definition in tool_registry.dart and SecurityPolicy (security_policy.dart:6-29) maps it to auto/permission/HITL. The gate is evaluated in Dart before execute: agent_cubit.dart:750-757 pauses on tier3Hitl and emits WaitingApproval; tool_registry.dart:250-253 re-checks checkPermission for tier2. The gateway RPC path (gateway_rpc_receiver.dart:143-148) also consults the registry, and its approval callback is requested per call (lines 110-140). I found no code path where a remote skill package, a tool result, a gateway frame, or model output writes to a tool's securityTier. Skill packages carry a free-text 'tier' YAML field (skills_registry_service.dart:50) but it is only a display string on the Skill entity — confirm it is not read by the tier gate. Residual: tier2 tools registered with a null checkPermission (ui_find_elements, read_web_page, nfc_read_tag, nfc_read_emoney_balance) execute with no registry permission check by design — that is a per-tool property, not a remote downgrade, and is covered by the individual tool entries."
          },
