          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/secrets-at-rest-in-plaintext-api-key-gateway-token-server-profiles",
          "ruleIndex": 30,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Secrets at rest in plaintext (API key, gateway token, server profiles) — Ruled out: lib/data/datasources/local/settings/secure_storage_service.dart + lib/common/injection/modules.dart\n\nFlutterSecureStorage is constructed with default AndroidOptions (lib/common/injection/modules.dart:23; lib/data/datasources/local/settings/secure_storage_service.dart:56-57). In flutter_secure_storage 9.2.4 the Android plugin then encrypts every value with AES-CBC-PKCS7 under an AES key RSA-wrapped by an AndroidKeyStore key (plugin FlutterSecureStorage.java write()/decodeRawValue(); ciphers/StorageCipher18Implementation.java, alias '<pkg>.FlutterSecureStoragePluginKey'); the init-failure fallback at ensureInitialized() still uses that cipher. No code path writes llm_api_key/server_profiles_list anywhere else. Control: plugin AES cipher at write() before editor.putString."
