          "ruleIndex": 34,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Intent redirection / state leakage via exported activity — Ruled out: RationaleActivity (exported, unguarded)\n\nRationaleActivity.kt:7-17 takes NO input from the launching intent (no getStringExtra, no getData, no nested Intent), unconditionally starts a hardcoded `androidx.health.ACTION_HEALTH_CONNECT_SETTINGS` intent, then finishes. It cannot be used as an intent-redirect trampoline (target is a constant), leaks no state, and grants no privileged action beyond opening Health Connect settings (which any app can already do via that public action). The only oddity is that it is exported without the START_VIEW_PERMISSION_USAGE permission that the ViewPermissionUsageActivity alias uses - a hygiene issue, not a reachable vulnerability, because the activity itself has no attacker-influenced behaviour."
          },
