        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/credential-storage-location-plaintext-fallback",
          "ruleIndex": 46,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Credential storage location / plaintext fallback — No issue identified: SecureStorageService (FlutterSecureStorage usage)\n\nConfirmed the entire app persists its credentials through FlutterSecureStorage only: SecureStorageService (lib/data/datasources/local/settings/secure_storage_service.dart) wraps FlutterSecureStorage for llm_api_key, llm_base_url, server_profiles_list and related settings, and DI instantiates it with default options at lib/common/injection/modules.dart:23. Searched for a fallback to plaintext stores for credential keys and found none. The plaintext SQLite/Hive stores hold chat content, memory vault rows and Action Center items, not credentials, so this is a storage-hygiene observation rather than a credential-exposure finding. NOTE: the default AndroidOptions of flutter_secure_storage 9.2.4 could not be confirmed from the pub cache (package not downloaded in this environment), so whether Android Keystore-backed encryption is applied by default is unverified - see open items."
          },
          "locations": [
