        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/unauthorized-ipc-service-hijack",
          "ruleIndex": 47,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Unauthorized IPC / service hijack — Ruled out: FlamesNotificationListenerService (permission-guarded, exported)\n\nThe BIND_NOTIFICATION_LISTENER_SERVICE gate at manifest:126 is the platform-enforced control: only the system (or a service the user explicitly enabled in Settings) can bind it, and the OS refuses third-party bind requests to that component. The service exposes no additional binder: it is a plain NotificationListenerService with only companion-object static state (FlamesNotificationListenerService.kt:17-36) reachable solely from MainActivity's own in-process MethodChannel handler (MainActivity.kt:124-135) - a third-party app has no channel to it. The buffer is in-memory only (notificationBuffer, :19)."
          },
          "locations": [
