            "text": "Unauthorized IPC / screen-content exposure — Ruled out: FlamesAccessibilityService (permission-guarded, exported)\n\nThe BIND_ACCESSIBILITY_SERVICE gate at manifest:136 is the platform-enforced control (user must enable the service in Settings; third-party bind is refused). The service exposes no binder of its own and no public static accessor that another app can call; its captured tree (FlamesAccessibilityService.kt:51-112) is only reachable through MainActivity's in-process channel (MainActivity.kt:186-190). accessibility_service_config.xml declares android:settingsActivity absent (no exported settings activity) and canRetrieveWindowContent=\"true\" - that is the intended read-only function of the user-enabled service, not a third-party reachable weakness. The service is read-only by design (no performAction calls - verified by rg)."
