          "message": {
            "text": "Overlay abuse / tapjacking / agent-state exposure via the floating bubble — Ruled out: FlamesOverlayBubble.kt + FlamesBackgroundService (SYSTEM_ALERT_WINDOW bubble)\n\nNamed controls: (a) the overlay service is declared android:exported=\"false\" (AndroidManifest.xml:157-164), so only this app can start it; (b) FlamesOverlayBubble.show() refuses to add the view unless Settings.canDrawOverlays() is true (FlamesOverlayBubble.kt:38) and the bubble is a bare 56dp ImageView whose only input handler (buildTouchListener, :105-161) calls the app's own onTap callback — it renders no agent state, no text, and exposes no data; (c) tapjacking cannot add authority because the tap only reaches handleBubbleTap (FlamesBackgroundService.kt:268-286), which starts/cancels a voice turn — the same action the user already performs deliberately, and the toggle is symmetric so a spurious tap is not a privilege gain. The bubble is only shown after the user grants SYSTEM_ALERT_WINDOW and enables the setting (overlay_bubble_service.dart:126-154)."
          },
