            "text": "Secret exposure through toString()/state serialization into logs or crash reports — Ruled out: Equatable toString of SettingsState / ServerProfile / GatewayAuthMessage and absence of crash/telemetry reporters\n\nequatable 2.1.0 EquatableConfig.stringify defaults to false (assert-enabled debug only), and GatewayAuthMessage.toString() therefore returns the bare type name; verified by reading the fetched package source (lib/src/equatable.dart:56-61, lib/src/equatable_config.dart). In addition, no BlocObserver/FlutterError.onError/runZonedGuarded handler is installed anywhere in lib/, so state objects carrying apiKey (SettingsState, SettingsData) are never serialized by a framework observer. dio 5.7.0 DioException.toString() prints only type/message/error (no headers, and RequestOptions has no toString override), so the Authorization header cannot reach FailureMessage.humanize's log call at failure_message.dart:18."
          },
