        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/cleartext-transport-sql-injection-in-local-datastores",
          "ruleIndex": 59,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Cleartext transport / SQL injection in local datastores — Ruled out: Semgrep local-ruleset triage (cleartext + SQL interpolation hits)\n\nRan a custom semgrep ruleset (the p/default and p/secrets registry packs were unreachable - semgrep.dev returned HTTP 500 and no cached rules existed). The cleartext rule produced exactly one hit, at lib/data/datasources/remote/settings/server_profile_probe_service_impl.dart:109, which is a ws:// to http:// scheme rewrite inside _normalizeHermesUrl, not a hardcoded cleartext endpoint. Confirmed no network_security_config and no usesCleartextTraffic attribute are declared, so Android 9+ blocks cleartext by default and the app fails closed. Also confirmed the SQL-injection-shaped hits were false positives: every database access uses bound parameters (the FTS MATCH query passes the sanitized term as a ? argument at sqlite_memory_datasource.dart:299, and the LIKE fallback builds only the fixed condition string while values go through whereArgs)."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
