        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/arbitrary-action-string-reaching-tool-execution-prompt-injection-through-the-action-channel",
          "ruleIndex": 61,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Arbitrary action string reaching tool execution / prompt injection through the action channel — Ruled out: lib/presentation/voice/voice_turn_action_listener.dart _handleAction — action string allowlist\n\nNamed control: the payload-to-action handler accepts only the three literals 'voice_input', 'cancel_voice', 'quick_status' after normalisation (lib/presentation/voice/voice_turn_action_listener.dart:162-178, switch on action.toLowerCase().trim()). Any other string, including a tool name or prompt, falls through with no effect — there is no path from this string into ToolRegistry.executeTool. So the action extra cannot name a tool or supply prompt text; it can only start the fixed mic turn or the fixed quick_status prompt. The consequence that DOES survive (an unauthenticated third-party app starting that turn without a tap) is tracked in its own coverage entry, because the control here bounds what the string can say, not who may say it."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
