        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/screen-level-surface-review-for-autonomous-action-credential-display-and-unsanitised-input",
          "ruleIndex": 62,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Screen-level surface review for autonomous action, credential display, and unsanitised input — No issue identified: Pocket Node, Node/Geofence screens, Gateway screens (pocket_node_screen.dart, geofence_management_screen.dart, gateway_link_cubit.dart, gateway_rpc_cubit.dart)\n\nReview scope: lib/presentation/screen/pocket_node/pocket_node_screen.dart, lib/presentation/screen/node/geofence_management_screen.dart + cubit, lib/presentation/screen/gateway/ (gateway_link_cubit.dart, gateway_rpc_cubit.dart). Findings: (a) pocket_node renders status only — endpoint, connection state, service list — and its diagnostic/ping handlers (pocket_node_screen.dart:397-420) are local UI stubs, with the endpoint taken from the stored active profile (:330-343) rather than from any input; no credential is displayed; (b) geofence entries are persisted through the same encrypted store (secure_storage_service.dart:338-343) and can be created by the tier-1 auto tool register_geofence (tool_registry.dart:968-975), but the only effect of a geofence is a local Action Center item with a display payload (ambient_trigger_service.dart:175-192), which the action-center entry already cleared as non-executing; (c) the gateway RPC cubit is the one surface where remote frames DO reach tool execution — that path is owned and covered by the gateway/tool-registry entries (tier gate at gateway_rpc_receiver.dart:88-104, execution at :143-152) and the read_web_page gate defect is filed under the share-intent entry. No new issue in this slice."
          },
