        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/credential-redirection-to-attacker-chosen-origin",
          "ruleIndex": 65,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Credential redirection to attacker-chosen origin — Ruled out: QR pairing persistence (ServerProfileCubit.addProfile / addFromPairingPayload)\n\nAdversarial re-test of the split-write negative; it holds on every path I could construct — no code path pairs a NEW base URL with a PRE-EXISTING stored key.\n\n(1) Writers of the stored base URL. `SecureStorageService.saveBaseUrl` (lib/data/datasources/local/settings/secure_storage_service.dart:59-61) is the only writer of `llm_base_url` (grep for `llm_base_url`/`keyBaseUrl` across lib/ returns nothing else). It has exactly three callers and each writes the key in the same operation: `saveSettings` (:131-148, key at :140), `setActiveServerProfile` (:281-288, key at :284), and `ServerProfileCubit.addProfile`'s `Future.wait` (server_profile_cubit.dart:140-145). The only other `saveApiKey` caller is `resetToDefaults`' clear (settings_cubit.dart:197). `resetToDefaults` (:189-210) writes `AppConstants.defaultBaseUrl` — a compile-time const `'https://api.openai.com/v1'` (lib/common/constant.dart:5) that no attacker input reaches — and preserving the key there keeps URL+credential matched (the key belongs to that origin); its only production caller is the AppBar reset button (settings_screen.dart:155). `saveServerProfile`/`saveServerProfiles` (secure_storage_service.dart:189-241) touch only the profile list, never `llm_base_url`; `deleteServerProfile` (:244-248) is reached only from `deleteProfile` (server_profile_cubit.dart:282) and re-syncs via `setActiveServerProfile` (:286), i.e. both fields together.\n\n(2) URL vs credential source. Every credential sink takes both from one call site: chat_datasource.dart:38-54 (baseUrl+apiKey params from the same AgentCubit snapshot, agent_cubit.dart:924-929, populated together at :481-492 from a single `getSettings()` read); server_profile_probe_service_impl.dart:23,70 (URL and token typed by the same user in the same form); voice_output_service.dart:227/255 (both from stored settings, with ZERO awaits between :227 and :255 — verified by counting, so no interleaving write can split the pair); gateway_client.dart:175-220 (token is the parameter passed with that URL; chat_screen.dart:1223 passes `payload.gatewayUrl`+`payload.token` from the same payload). No Interceptor, no default `Options`/`BaseOptions` header and no `HttpClient` exists anywhere in lib/ (modules.dart:14-17 sets timeouts only; `Interceptor` has zero hits), so nothing can attach a stored key to a request whose URL came from elsewhere.\n\n(3) `ServerProfile.copyWith` (server_profile.dart:28-49) allows single-field updates, so I read every call site: secure_storage_service.dart:220/230/272/276 pass only `isActive`; server_profile_cubit.dart:318 passes only `lastConnected`; server_profile_cubit.dart:235-240 passes `gatewayUrl` AND `token` together from the same form submit (settings_screen.dart:144-149). No site replaces `gatewayUrl` while retaining a prior `token`.\n\n(4) Non-pairing routes: manual paste is the same `_handleBarcode` path (qr_scanner_screen.dart:250); Add-Profile (add_profile_screen.dart:411-425) creates a new profile with `makeActive:false` (addProfile :139 only syncs when it becomes active, and then writes both from that form); `MainActivity.extractActionFromIntent` (MainActivity.kt:73-85) reads only `extra_flames_action` into a fixed three-value switch (voice_turn_action_listener.dart:162-178); the share path (share_target_cubit.dart, share_target_service.dart) maps payloads to chat prompts only; `GatewayDeviceRpcReceiver.handleRequest` (gateway_rpc_receiver.dart:68-176) only calls `toolRegistry.executeTool`, and no registered tool writes base URL/key.\n\nI could not name any control that fails on these paths because none exists — the control is structural: the two values are always written and read as a matched pair from one payload/source."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "QR pairing persistence (ServerProfileCubit.addProfile / addFromPairingPayload)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "strix": {
              "coverage_outcome": "ruled_out",
              "risk_area": "Credential redirection to attacker-chosen origin",
              "surface": "QR pairing persistence (ServerProfileCubit.addProfile / addFromPairingPayload)",
              "recorded_by": "Split-Write Credential Exfil Adversary",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/alternative-config-write-path-with-weaker-validation-intent-deep-link-manual-entry",
