          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Auto-enable of an imported remote skill (untrusted text entering the system prompt without user opt-in) — Ruled out: Skill enablement state: applyImportPolicy → persistence → hydrateFromStorage re-enable path (lib/domain/services/skills/skills_registry_service.dart:134-178, :188-217, :249-257; lib/data/datasources/local/skills/skills_local_datasource.dart:150-171)\n\nControl: applyImportPolicy at skill_security_scanner.dart:189-190 forces `isEnabled: false, isCommunity: true` on every imported skill, and SkillImportService.confirmImport is the only production caller of registerImportedSkill (skill_import_service.dart:70). Swept the re-enable paths: setSkillEnabled (:249-257) is reachable only from SkillsCubit.toggleSkill, which is wired only to the user-facing toggle in skills_hub_screen.dart:313-327; hydrateFromStorage/_hydrate (:163-170) applies loadSkillStates() from the `skill_states` table, but that table is written by saveSkillState with the already-false value at registerImportedSkill (:213), and saveSkillState is otherwise called only from _persistSkillState under an explicit user toggle (:254). registerSkillFromMarkdown/registerSkill have NO production UI caller (grep: only skills_cubit.dart:113-120 definitions plus tests). So an imported skill cannot become active without a deliberate user tap."
