        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/tool-privilege-escalation-via-a-remote-skill-s-tools-list-tier-change-from-skill-frontmatter",
          "ruleIndex": 68,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Tool-privilege escalation via a remote skill's `tools` list / tier change from skill frontmatter — Ruled out: SkillsRegistryService.syncWithToolRegistry + ToolRegistry enable/disable state (lib/domain/services/skills/skills_registry_service.dart:386-405, lib/domain/tools/chat/tool_registry.dart:208-222)\n\nControl: a skill's `tools` list is consumed only by syncWithToolRegistry (skills_registry_service.dart:386-405), which calls setToolEnabled(name, true) at :403 for active skills and setToolEnabled(name, false) at :397 only for tools of INACTIVE skills that no active skill claims. Since ToolRegistry.register does `_toolEnabledStates.putIfAbsent(tool.name, () => true)` (tool_registry.dart:210) and isToolEnabled defaults `?? true` (:222), every registered tool starts enabled, so a skill naming an already-registered tool grants nothing the user did not already have. Unknown tool names are the one rejection path (skill_security_scanner.dart:178-184) and no UI exposes a tool-enable toggle (grep for setToolEnabled in lib/presentation/ returns nothing), so a skill cannot override a user's manual disable choice either."
          },
          "locations": [
