        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/remote-frame-re-points-stored-credential-bypasses-tool-tier-gate",
          "ruleIndex": 69,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Remote frame re-points stored credential / bypasses tool tier gate — Ruled out: Gateway WebSocket JSON-RPC frame handling (GatewayDeviceRpcReceiver / GatewayRpcCubit)\n\n`GatewayDeviceRpcReceiver.handleRequest` (`lib/domain/services/gateway/gateway_rpc_receiver.dart:68-176`) only calls `toolRegistry.executeTool(request.tool, request.arguments)`, and no registered tool writes endpoint configuration: grepping `saveBaseUrl|saveApiKey|saveSettings|saveServerProfile` across `lib/domain` and `lib/data/datasources/tools` returns no writer (only `voice_output_service.dart`/`overlay_bubble_service.dart` read SecureStorageService). The RPC frame schema carries `tool` + `arguments` only. Tier-3 tools do gate: `gateway_rpc_cubit.dart:149-155` emits `GatewayRpcWaitingApproval` and blocks on a Completer until the user approves or rejects. What the gateway DOES gain is durable device-tool authority (tool manifest sent post-auth, `gateway_client.dart:301-303`), which is part of the pairing finding rather than a separate config-redirection bug."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "Gateway WebSocket JSON-RPC frame handling (GatewayDeviceRpcReceiver / GatewayRpcCubit)"
