          "message": {
            "text": "Camera frame upload to an unvalidated/attacker-chosen URL — Not applicable: External camera (UVC) preview + capture, and camera_take_photo\n\nCamera frames never touch a network path in the app's own code: external_camera_service.dart contains no http/url/socket/upload references (grep returns nothing) and the plugin is flutter_ffi_uvc ^1.0.0 (pubspec.yaml:41). The preview is a local Flutter texture created and attached in external_camera_preview_cubit.dart:118-162; a still frame is captured and returned as raw base64 JPEG (tool_registry.dart:520-524) which becomes a tool result to the user's own configured LLM. There is no URL for frames at all, so the 'is the frame upload URL validated' question is not applicable. camera_take_photo (built-in) is likewise tier2Permission with only a permission check and no alternate endpoint."
          },
