        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/tool-tier-gate-bypass-invoking-a-tier-3-tool-without-hitl-or-downgrading-a-tier-from-remote-input",
          "ruleIndex": 73,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Tool tier-gate bypass — invoking a Tier-3 tool without HITL, or downgrading a tier from remote input — Ruled out: Tier enforcement points: agent_cubit.dart:742-762 (approval gate + dispatch), tool_registry.dart:238-262 (executeTool), gateway_rpc_receiver.dart:89-151, tool_call_text_parser.dart:214-235\n\nControl: the HITL gate is a direct equality test on the tier constant stored at registration — `if (registered.securityTier == SecurityTier.tier3Hitl)` at agent_cubit.dart:753, with `registered` from `_toolRegistry.getTool(toolName)` (:730). securityTier is set literally per RegisteredTool in tool_registry.dart (verified for all 44 registrations by scripted extraction: 24 tier1Auto / 16 tier2Permission / 4 tier3Hitl) and is never read from a gateway frame, skill frontmatter, tool result, or model-supplied parameter. Skill frontmatter `tier` is parsed (skills_registry_service.dart:50) but referenced ONLY in display widgets. The fallback text tool-call parser (tool_call_text_parser.dart:214-235) cannot reach a tool that the model could not already call: it validates against `isKnownTool` and then hands off to the same _processPendingToolCalls gate. Gateway RPC path also gates Tier 3 before executing (gateway_rpc_receiver.dart:89-143) and fails closed when no approval callback is wired (:91-104)."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "Tier enforcement points: agent_cubit.dart:742-762 (approval gate + dispatch), tool_registry.dart:238-262 (executeTool), gateway_rpc_receiver.dart:89-151, tool_call_text_parser.dart:214-235"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
