        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/remote-skill-text-entering-the-system-prompt-without-user-opt-in",
          "ruleIndex": 74,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Remote skill text entering the system prompt without user opt-in — Ruled out: SkillsRegistryService.buildSystemPrompt (lib/domain/services/skills/skills_registry_service.dart:331-382) consumed at agent_cubit.dart:916-921\n\nControl: buildSystemPrompt is only reachable for skills where `isEnabled == true` — `getActiveSkills()` filters `.where((s) => s.isEnabled)` (skills_registry_service.dart:296-297) and buildSystemPrompt returns `basePrompt ?? ''` when the active list is empty (:333-336). Combined with applyImportPolicy forcing isEnabled=false (:189-190) and the ruled-out re-enable path (entry d1b975), a freshly imported community skill contributes NOTHING to the system prompt until the user explicitly enables it. What remains is the residual fact that enabled-skill text is concatenated verbatim at :362-379 with no delimiter (consumed at agent_cubit.dart:916-921) — recorded as an observation attached to the import-pipeline entry d68232 rather than as a separate finding, since the entry precondition is a deliberate user action."
          },
