              "surface": "FlamesAccessibilityService — window-content exposure and settingsActivity",
              "recorded_by": "Validate MainActivity Action Injection",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/remote-controlled-tier-downgrade-gateway-frame-skill-package-tool-result-mutating-a-tool-s-tier",
          "ruleIndex": 78,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Remote-controlled tier downgrade (gateway frame / skill package / tool result mutating a tool's tier) — Ruled out: ToolRegistry tier resolution + SecurityTier assignment paths\n\n`RegisteredTool.securityTier` is a `final SecurityTier` set only from compile-time constants in tool_registry.dart (e.g. :708, :742, :899) and RegisteredTool's const constructor (:53-60). Verified no remote input can write it: the only SecurityTier assignment outside tool_registry.dart is doc_builder_skill.dart:62 (a local constant). Skill frontmatter `tier` is display-only metadata, not consulted by any gate (grep `securityTier` across lib/domain/services/skills/, lib/data/datasources/skills/, lib/data/datasources/remote/skills/ returns only doc_builder_skill.dart:62). The tier read at agent_cubit.dart:753 comes from `_toolRegistry.getTool(toolName)` (:730) → the local registered constant. So the gate decision itself cannot be downgraded by a gateway frame, skill package, or tool result."
          },
