          "message": {
            "text": "Sensitive data exposure — password field text captured from other apps — Requires further review: FlamesAccessibilityService.captureTree() password/secure-field handling\n\ncaptureTree() never calls AccessibilityNodeInfo.isPassword(); the identifier appears nowhere in the android/ or lib/ trees (repo-wide search). Whether the platform already redacts password text before an accessibility service sees it is device/OEM dependent and could NOT be verified — no device, no emulator, no adb. The missing client-side control is established; actual secret capture is not. Fix included as a second part of vuln-0004 (skips isPassword nodes and their subtrees); device verification of both the gap and the fix remains open."
