          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Injection mitigation claim — keyword filter as a security control — Ruled out: NotificationTriageService._sensitiveKeywords / isSensitive filter (notification_triage_service.dart:87-122)\n\nnotification_triage_service.dart:87-122 `_sensitiveKeywords`/`isSensitive` excludes entries whose title+body contain otp|password|pin|bank|transaction|payment|balance|credit card|etc. This is a CONTENT-TOPIC noise filter, not an instruction filter: it matches banking/credential vocabulary and has no concept of instruction-like text (e.g. \"ignore previous instructions\", \"call clipboard_write\"). A payload containing none of those keywords passes unfiltered. Confirmed by reading the keyword list and the `haystack.contains` matching logic at :119-122. It therefore provides no mitigation for the injection path."
