            "text": "Tier-2 gate bypass / unvalidated URL launcher reachable from model output — Ruled out: open_external_url (tool_registry.dart:1418-1435)\n\nShape (b) form (no justifying comment at :1432) BUT neutralised: `contact_launcher_tools.dart:159-163` rejects anything that is not http/https with a non-empty host before `canLaunchUrl`/`launchUrl`, so `intent://`, `market://`, `javascript:`, `file:`, `tel:` are all rejected. No Android runtime permission exists for opening a browser URL, so the absent `checkPermission` skips no permission evaluation. Residual (noted, not claimed): the tool is auto-executable, so model output can pop a browser at an arbitrary https URL with no confirmation — low-severity UI effect, no unauthorized data access."
