          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Tier-2 gate bypass / privilege-chaining via system settings launcher — Ruled out: launch_system_setting (tool_registry.dart:1502-1527)\n\nShape (b) form (no justifying comment at :1524) BUT neutralised on both sides: Dart allow-list at `intent_launcher_service_impl.dart:223` (`_allowedSettings.contains(normalized)` -> ServerFailure) and Kotlin `when` at `MainActivity.kt:431-446` with `else -> null` -> `result.success(false)`. No Android runtime permission exists for launching a settings page, so the absent `checkPermission` skips no permission evaluation. Residual (assessed, low): the allow-list deliberately INCLUDES `accessibility`, `notification_listener` and `overlay` (`system_settings_allow_list.dart:40-44`, documented as intentional per AGENTS.md §7), and the tool auto-executes, so model/injected text can walk the user to the privilege-granting page with no confirmation — a UI-spoofing/social-engineering primitive, but the user must still perform the toggle, so no unauthorized grant occurs. Mis-tiering (should be Tier 3 HITL) is a distinct root cause, routed to the Tier-1/mis-tiering agent rather than duplicated here."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "launch_system_setting (tool_registry.dart:1502-1527)"
                }
              ]
            }
