          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/tier-2-gate-bypass-unauthorized-message-composition",
          "ruleIndex": 90,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Tier-2 gate bypass / unauthorized message composition — Ruled out: open_email_composer (tool_registry.dart:1471-1499)\n\nShape (b) form (silent omission, no justifying comment at :1493) BUT no Android runtime permission exists for composing an email, so the absent `checkPermission` skips no permission evaluation. The sensitive act (sending) is not performed by the app: `intent_launcher_service_impl.dart:190-205` only builds a `mailto:` URI and calls `launchUrl`; the message is a prefill the user must explicitly send from their mail client. Residual (noted, low): the tool auto-executes, so model/injected text can prefill an outbound email (to/subject/body) with no confirmation — a phishing/social-engineering affordance, not an unauthorized send."
          },
