        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/tier-2-gate-bypass-unauthorized-nfc-tag-read",
          "ruleIndex": 91,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Tier-2 gate bypass / unauthorized NFC tag read — Ruled out: nfc_read_tag (tool_registry.dart:1558-1602)\n\nShape (b) form (silent omission, no justifying comment at :1568) BUT there is no runtime permission to evaluate: `android.permission.NFC` is an install-time (normal) permission — Android never shows a runtime dialog for it — and the app declares no runtime NFC permission path. The real gate is physical presence: `nfc_service.dart:260-265` `readCardUid` calls `_platform.scan(...)` and `DefaultNfcPlatformWrapper.runWithCard/scan` (nfc_service.dart:70-80) start an `NfcManager` foreground dispatch session with a 20s timeout that only completes when the user physically taps a tag into the field. A headless invocation cannot read a card without the user presenting one, and the tool's `execute` closure additionally checks `isAvailable()`/`isEnabled()` before scanning. Absent `checkPermission` therefore skips nothing."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "nfc_read_tag (tool_registry.dart:1558-1602)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
