        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/tier-2-gate-bypass-covert-camera-capture-without-permission",
          "ruleIndex": 93,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Tier-2 gate bypass / covert camera capture without permission — Ruled out: camera_take_photo (tool_registry.dart:354-379)\n\nShape (b) form (silent omission, no justifying comment at :371) BUT the OS gate covers it: `camera_vision_service.dart:73-79` calls `image_picker` `pickImage(source: ImageSource.camera)`, which launches the system camera Activity as a foreground UI the user must operate, and because the app declares `android.permission.CAMERA` (AndroidManifest.xml:14) Android enforces that permission for the capture intent. A denial surfaces as `PermissionFailure` at `camera_vision_service.dart:100-107` (PlatformException permission mapping). The contrast tool's checker is check-only anyway (`external_camera_service.dart:265-267` -> `Permission.camera.status`, no request), so the omitted pre-check changes only the error message, not the authority. `retrieveLostData()` (:50-68) re-surfaces an image the user already captured in a prior session, not a new covert capture."
          },
