        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/unbounded-download-resource-exhaustion-recursive-delete-via-attacker-influenced-voiceid",
          "ruleIndex": 100,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Unbounded download / resource exhaustion; recursive-delete via attacker-influenced voiceId — No issue identified: PiperVoiceStore.downloadVoice network fetch (piper_tts_engine.dart:188-229) and PiperVoiceStore.deleteVoice (piper_tts_engine.dart:275-290)\n\nNo realistic attacker control on either path. The fetch URL is the hardcoded k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx GitHub HTTPS release (piper_voice.dart:36-37) and `tarballSizeBytes` is declared but never enforced anywhere (grep: only the const definitions) — an unbounded-download/DoS concern only against a compromised GitHub origin, outside the threat model, so recorded as robustness, not a finding. `deleteVoice` does `Directory(_joinPath(modelsRoot, voiceId)).delete(recursive: true)` (:277-280) with no `..`/separator check on `voiceId`, but every caller supplies a catalog id from `kPiperVoiceCatalog` (settings_screen.dart:832, :846 via settings_cubit.dart:472-480, :612-623) and `piper_voice_id` in secure storage has no remote writer (only settings_screen.dart:730 → settings_cubit.dart:438). Not attacker-reachable; latent robustness gap only."
          },
          "locations": [
