        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/insecure-deserialization-object-injection-from-attacker-controlled-skill-package",
          "ruleIndex": 102,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Insecure deserialization / object injection from attacker-controlled skill package — Ruled out: lib/data/datasources/remote/skills/skill_remote_loader.dart + lib/domain/services/skills/skills_registry_service.dart:32-117 (SKILL.md ingest and parse)\n\nINDEPENDENTLY RE-CONFIRMED (ruled_out unchanged; evidence materially extended). Re-ran the parse path against the real pinned `yaml` 3.1.4 with 20 adversarial frontmatter documents, executing `parseSkillFromMarkdown` (skills_registry_service.dart:36-115) verbatim.\n\nKey precision the original entry lacked: the parser does NOT sanitise — it ACCEPTS hostile identifiers and passes them through. Confirmed accepted values: `id: ../../evil` → `Skill.id == \"../../evil\"`; `id: /etc/passwd` → `Skill.id == \"/etc/passwd\"`; `id: sub/dir/skill`; the no-frontmatter heading fallback at :99-114 yields `# ../../evil` → `id == \"../../evil\"` and `# a/b/c` → `id == \"a/b/c\"`. So the negative is \"hostile value accepted but no sink\", NOT \"hostile value rejected\".\n\nYAML-specific vectors executed, all benign: anchor/alias reuse (S5) and a 9-level nested alias fan-out (S6) expand to a bounded scalar/string form and cannot execute or allocate unboundedly — the values only ever reach `.toString()` at :45-56. Duplicate mapping keys throw `Error on line 2, column 1: Duplicate mapping key` and are caught by the `catch (_)` at :79, falling back to the heading parser — no crash, no partial-object state. Non-scalar `id` (a map) stringifies to `\"{nested: value}\"`; numeric `12345`/boolean `true` coerce via `.toString()`. `tools: clipboard_read` (scalar, not list) is ignored because of the `is YamlList` guard at :59, so a scalar cannot become a tool entry; a nested list `[[clipboard_read]]` becomes the literal string `\"[clipboard_read]\"`, which cannot match any registered tool name and is therefore rejected by the unknown-tools gate (`SkillScanResult.hasUnknownTools`, skill_scan.dart:41-45). A 5000-element `tools` list parses without error. A NUL in a quoted scalar survives as a literal character; no truncation-based bypass.\n\nSink re-verification (the reason this stays ruled_out): a full-tree search of the skills pipeline — `lib/data/datasources/local/skills/`, `lib/domain/services/skills/`, `lib/data/datasources/remote/skills/`, `lib/data/datasources/skills/`, `lib/presentation/screen/skills/`, `lib/domain/entities/skills/` — for `File(`/`Directory(`/`writeAs`/`openWrite`/`createSync`/`.join(`/`$dir` returns exactly ONE hit: `File(path).parent.create(recursive: true)` at skills_local_datasource.dart:63, where `path` comes from `sqflite`'s `getDatabasesPath()`/`_databasePath` (the app-private database dir, :52-57) and is never derived from skill data. `skill.id`/`skill.name` are used only as a `Map<String, Skill>` key (skills_registry_service.dart:120-122, :201-213) and as a bound SQLite primary key (`where: 'id = ?'` / `whereArgs`, skills_local_datasource.dart:144-148, :165-170). The skill loader also has no import of or reference to `PiperVoiceStore`/`downloadVoice`, so it cannot reach the tarball extraction path either."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "lib/data/datasources/remote/skills/skill_remote_loader.dart + lib/domain/services/skills/skills_registry_service.dart:32-117 (SKILL.md ingest and parse)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "strix": {
              "coverage_outcome": "ruled_out",
              "risk_area": "Insecure deserialization / object injection from attacker-controlled skill package",
              "surface": "lib/data/datasources/remote/skills/skill_remote_loader.dart + lib/domain/services/skills/skills_registry_service.dart:32-117 (SKILL.md ingest and parse)",
              "recorded_by": "Tar Extraction Bypass Validator",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/path-traversal-arbitrary-file-write-from-package-supplied-identifiers",
          "ruleIndex": 103,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Path traversal / arbitrary file write from package-supplied identifiers — Ruled out: Skill package id/name → filesystem path (skills_registry_service.dart:188-217, doc_builder_skill.dart:91-99)\n\nNo path is constructed from package-supplied strings. `skill.id`/`skill.name` are used only as a `Map<String, Skill>` key and SQLite primary key (skills_registry_service.dart:120-122, :201-213; local datasource insert at :132-141 uses bound `where: 'id = ?'`/column values, never interpolation). Grep for `File(`/`Directory(` across lib/domain/services/skills/, lib/data/datasources/local/skills/, lib/data/datasources/remote/skills/ and lib/presentation/screen/skills/ returns no file-write sites. The one adjacent write is doc_builder_skill.dart:91-99, whose `outputFileName`/title is passed through `_slugify` (:125-132) that replaces every char outside [a-z0-9] with '_' and caps at 60 chars, so traversal cannot survive into `<documents>/documents/doc_<slug>_<stamp>.pdf`. A skill package also cannot name a URL: `sourceUrl` comes from the user-typed field (skill_import_dialog.dart:108-110), not from package content."
