            "text": "Code execution / native-library loading from extracted archive content — Not applicable: Extracted Piper model directory (sherpa_onnx consumption path, piper_tts_engine.dart:56-88, 336-357)\n\nNo code-execution primitive exists on the extracted content: grep across lib/ for `Process.run|Process.start|chmod|DynamicLibrary|dlopen|loadLibrary|open(` returns nothing, and no Kotlin code handles archives. The extracted `.onnx`/`tokens.txt`/`espeak-ng-data` are consumed only as data-file paths by `sherpa_onnx.OfflineTtsVitsModelConfig` (piper_tts_engine.dart:66-74); the native library itself ships with the app, is not loaded from the extraction directory, and the model files are parsed as data, not executed. So even a hypothetical arbitrary write into that directory would not be an RCE path on its own."
