        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/tls-certificate-validation-bypass-missing-pinning-for-credential-bearing-requests",
          "ruleIndex": 108,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "TLS certificate validation bypass / missing pinning for credential-bearing requests — Ruled out: Dio configuration (lib/common/injection/modules.dart:13-17) and all credential-bearing HTTPS clients\n\nClient-side TLS verification is left at the platform default: no Dio HttpClientAdapter, no badCertificateCallback, no SecurityContext or certificate-pinning configuration exists anywhere in lib/ (grep for HttpClientAdapter|badCertificateCallback|SecurityContext returns nothing; NetworkModule.provideDio at lib/common/injection/modules.dart:13-17 sets only timeouts). Credentials therefore ride on the same OS-validated TLS as every other request, and a MITM would need a user-installed CA; that is the platform baseline rather than an application defect."
          },
