        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/tier-gate-bypass-tier-downgrade-by-remote-input",
          "ruleIndex": 109,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Tier-gate bypass / tier downgrade by remote input — Ruled out: Tier resolution for read_device_file and list_device_files (tool_registry.dart registration + agent_cubit.dart gate)\n\nThe tier is read from the local `securityTier` constant on the RegisteredTool at registration (tool_registry.dart:782 and :809) and consumed by the HITL gate at agent_cubit.dart:760-765 and the permission gate at tool_registry.dart:250-255. No remote input (gateway frame, skill package, tool result, model argument) writes to RegisteredTool.securityTier — no such setter exists. So the tier itself cannot be downgraded. The real defect is not a downgrade but that list_device_files is *declared* tier1Auto in the source, and read_device_file's tier2 gate is a no-op; both are covered by the file-read finding."
          },
