        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/broad-external-storage-read-claimed-sdcard-access",
          "ruleIndex": 110,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Broad external-storage read (claimed /sdcard access) — Ruled out: External-storage read reachability via read_device_file (AndroidManifest.xml:3-36)\n\nConfirmed no READ_EXTERNAL_STORAGE / MANAGE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE / WRITE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE anywhere in android/ (grep across the whole android tree returns nothing; AndroidManifest.xml:3-36 lists only INTERNET, calendar, location, camera, contacts, NFC, Health Connect, audio, notifications). Consequence: on modern Android the model cannot read /sdcard — scoped storage + absence of the permission makes those reads fail with EACCES. This genuinely limits the finding's blast radius and is recorded as counterevidence; it does NOT remove the finding, because the app's own private storage (databases/, app_flutter/, shared_prefs/, files/) is fully readable by the same UID with no permission required, and that is where the plaintext SQLite databases live."
          },
          "locations": [
