        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/full-plaintext-chat-transcript-disclosure",
          "ruleIndex": 111,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Full plaintext chat-transcript disclosure — Ruled out: Chat history at rest (flames_chat.db) readability by read_device_file\n\nSuperseded by a stronger conclusion from a later self-check. The plaintext SQLite databases are NOT readable via read_device_file at all, blocked twice over: (1) `db` and `sqlite` are both present in `_binaryExtensions` (file_workspace_service.dart:98-124); (2) a real SQLite file has a NUL byte at offset 15 of its header (`SQLite format 3\\x00`), and `_containsNullByte` (:133-140) scans the first 8000 bytes and rejects it independently of the filename. I also confirmed chat message bodies are not in the DB (they are in FlutterSecureStorage, chat_local_datasource.dart:113-125) and that memory-vault content is already model-accessible via the Tier-1 list_memories/search_memories tools (tool_registry.dart:905-945), so file-level access to those DBs would add nothing. My earlier claim that the denylist \"does not protect the plaintext databases\" was an overclaim; corrected in report vuln-0007."
          },
