          "ruleIndex": 114,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Credential forwarding to a redirect target chosen by the configured base URL (dio followRedirects default) — Ruled out: DioTtsClient.synthesize (lib/data/datasources/tools/chat/voice_output_service.dart:219-272) — Authorization: Bearer on the TTS request\n\nRESOLVED for the redirect question this entry was opened on: ruled out. The stored API key attached to the TTS request (voice_output_service.dart:255-258) is not forwarded across a cross-origin redirect, because dart:io's `shouldCopyHeaderOnRedirect` strips the `authorization` header unless the redirect target is same-scheme/host/port. The separate cleartext-transport exposure of the same request (a non-TLS stored base URL, not a redirect) is real and is filed as vuln-0009 (medium, CVSS 5.9) together with the TLS-only fix covering this client."
