          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/tls-certificate-validation-disabled-trust-store-bypass",
          "ruleIndex": 117,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "TLS certificate validation disabled / trust store bypass — Ruled out: Dio configuration (lib/common/injection/modules.dart) and all HTTP/WS client construction\n\nSearched the whole tree for TLS overrides: no `badCertificateCallback`, `onBadCertificate`, `setTrustedCertificates`, `SecurityContext`, `HttpOverrides`, `onHttpClientCreate`, or `createHttpClient` in `lib/` or `android/`; the only hits are `lib/common/failure_message.dart:69` and a test asserting a humanized message. The shared Dio (`lib/common/injection/modules.dart:14-17`) sets only connectTimeout/receiveTimeout and registers no interceptors. Certificate validation therefore runs dart:io defaults against the system trust store. No `wss`->`ws` downgrade on reconnect (see reconnect entry)."
          },
