        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/sse-parser-injection-unbounded-buffering-script-execution-from-remote-text",
          "ruleIndex": 118,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "SSE parser injection / unbounded buffering / script execution from remote text — No issue identified: lib/data/datasources/remote/chat/sse_parser.dart + chat_datasource.dart streaming path\n\n`SseParser.parse` (sse_parser.dart:78-106) only accepts lines whose trimmed form starts with the literal `data:` (:88), takes the substring after it (:92), and passes it to `jsonDecode` inside a try that swallows only FormatException (:97-102). The caller splits the byte stream on newlines first (chat_datasource.dart:63-68), so a crafted `data:` payload cannot escape JSON parsing into an interpreter, and unparseable frames are dropped. The stream is consumed incrementally by the Dio ResponseBody stream (chat_datasource.dart:38,63) rather than buffered to completion; the model's delta content is rendered through `MarkdownBody` (chat_screen.dart:2078, 2175, 2218) which emits Flutter widgets and does not execute HTML/JS — no WebView is used anywhere (no webview dependency in pubspec.yaml)."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "lib/data/datasources/remote/chat/sse_parser.dart + chat_datasource.dart streaming path"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "strix": {
              "coverage_outcome": "no_issue_found",
              "risk_area": "SSE parser injection / unbounded buffering / script execution from remote text",
              "surface": "lib/data/datasources/remote/chat/sse_parser.dart + chat_datasource.dart streaming path",
              "recorded_by": "Gateway Transport And Token Attach",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/inbound-frame-type-with-unexpected-side-effect-url-fetch-profile-change-file-write",
          "ruleIndex": 119,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Inbound frame type with unexpected side effect (URL fetch, profile change, file write) — No issue identified: lib/domain/services/gateway/gateway_rpc_receiver.dart + all gateway frame types\n\nEnumerated every inbound frame type in gateway_message.dart:16-81 and traced each side effect: `tool_call_request`/`tool_call` -> tool execution (covered by the dedicated SSRF candidate); `elicitation_request` -> UI approval only, auto-rejected on timeout (gateway_rpc_cubit.dart:191-215); `text_delta`/`chat_message`/`tool_event`/`error` -> UI state and `MarkdownBody` text only (chat_screen.dart:288-362); `ping` -> pong; `auth_*` -> connection state. No frame type carries a URL, profile mutation, or file path (verified by grep for url/baseUrl/gatewayUrl in the entity file: zero hits), so no frame can redirect a credential or trigger a fetch to a frame-supplied destination. The one real privilege crossing is the tool-call path, handled separately."
          },
