        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/credential-attach-without-origin-validation-connection-probe",
          "ruleIndex": 120,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Credential attach without origin validation (connection probe) — Ruled out: lib/data/datasources/remote/settings/server_profile_probe_service_impl.dart probeHermesNode / probeOpenAi\n\nResolved by enumerating all callers: `ServerProfileProbeService` is only reached from `add_profile_screen.dart:361-393` (`_onTestConnection`, the explicit user-initiated \"Test connection\" button), and `probeService` is constructed solely at `injection.dart:24-27`. The credential passed in is the value the user just typed into the token field (`add_profile_screen.dart:363,387,389`) — no stored secret is ever fed to it. So there is no silent-exfiltration path here: the user chooses the origin and supplies the credential in the same action, which is the normal, intended behavior of a connection test. Not a vulnerability."
