        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/stored-api-key-attached-to-a-stored-base-url-with-no-origin-binding",
          "ruleIndex": 121,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Stored API key attached to a stored base URL with no origin binding — Ruled out: lib/data/datasources/tools/chat/voice_output_service.dart DioTtsClient (remote TTS)\n\nResolved by adjacent work. The redirect half is ruled out: dart:io's shouldCopyHeaderOnRedirect strips authorization on cross-origin redirects, confirmed by the cleartext lane (entry 98ec17). The cleartext half is filed as vuln-0009 (credentials over http:///ws://, incl. the TTS endpoint), and entry efff3e covers this exact sink. What remains is the general \"stored key attached to a stored URL with no origin binding\" property, which is the same defect already reported for the chat path — there is no separate defect in the TTS client beyond it, and the stored URL/key can only be written through the user-driven settings and profile flows (settings_cubit.dart:117-121, server_profile_cubit.dart:97-107), both of which require http/https with a non-empty host. Not re-filed to avoid duplicating vuln-0009."
          },
