        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/weaker-validation-alternative-path-to-set-the-active-base-url-deep-link-exported-activity-gateway-rpc-manual-form",
          "ruleIndex": 122,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Weaker-validation alternative path to set the active base URL (deep link / exported activity / gateway RPC / manual form) — Ruled out: Non-QR base-URL configuration writers (settings reset, Add-Profile form, exported-activity extras, gateway RPC tools)\n\nRuled out by enumerating every writer of the gateway destination. `saveBaseUrl(`/`saveApiKey(` appear in lib/ only as matched pairs: secure_storage_service.dart:139-140 (saveSettings) and :283-284 (setActiveServerProfile), and server_profile_cubit.dart:141-142 (addProfile, both from the same payload), plus the settings reset to defaults at settings_cubit.dart:192-197. No registered tool writes the base URL or API key (grep for saveBaseUrl|saveApiKey|saveSettings over lib/domain and lib/data/datasources/tools is empty), so the paired gateway cannot re-point the destination through the tool channel. The exported MainActivity path surfaces only a fixed three-value action allowlist consumed by VoiceTurnActionListener, with no extra reaching storage. The Add-Profile form uses the stricter shared predicate `isAcceptableGatewayUrl` (lib/domain/services/gateway/gateway_url.dart:39-52, called at add_profile_screen.dart:163 and :365), which is user-typed rather than payload-supplied. No deep link or intent filter sets a server profile."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
