        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/credential-forwarding-across-a-cross-origin-redirect",
          "ruleIndex": 123,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Credential forwarding across a cross-origin redirect — Ruled out: chat_datasource / voice_output_service / probe redirect handling (followRedirects default true)\n\nChecked whether the credential could leak through a redirect. dart:io's `_HttpClient.shouldCopyHeaderOnRedirect` (sdk/lib/_http/http_impl.dart, `_openUrlFromRequest`) strips `authorization`, `www-authenticate`, `proxy-authorization`, `proxy-authenticate`, `cookie` and `cookie2` unless `_isSameOrigin` (scheme + host + port all equal) holds — so an `https` credential request redirected to a third-party origin does NOT carry the bearer token. This closes the \"open redirect leaks the key\" variant. Note this does not help the cleartext case (that is a direct request to a non-TLS origin, filed as vuln-0009). dio's default `followRedirects: true` therefore does not add a separate credential-exfil path here."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "chat_datasource / voice_output_service / probe redirect handling (followRedirects default true)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "strix": {
              "coverage_outcome": "ruled_out",
              "risk_area": "Credential forwarding across a cross-origin redirect",
              "surface": "chat_datasource / voice_output_service / probe redirect handling (followRedirects default true)",
              "recorded_by": "Cleartext Credential Transport Validator",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/sending-credentials-to-a-url-taken-from-an-inbound-message",
          "ruleIndex": 124,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Sending credentials to a URL taken from an inbound message — Ruled out: All outbound gateway/LLM send paths (gateway_client.dart sendJson/sendChatMessage + callers)\n\nTraced every outbound gateway send: `sendJson` (gateway_client.dart:391-394) is only ever called with locally constructed messages (auth frame :216, pong :263, tool manifest :303, tool responses :399-423, chat :427-437, cancel :441-443), and `sendChatMessage` has exactly two callers (`chat_screen.dart:1522` gated on `client.state.isConnected`, and `gateway_voice_prompt_dispatcher.dart:74`). No outbound frame destination or credential is derived from an inbound frame, and no frame type carries a URL/host (verified by grep against `lib/domain/entities/gateway/gateway_message.dart`: zero hits for url/baseUrl/gatewayUrl). The only URL-bearing outbound calls are the local LLM/TTS clients, whose base URL comes from secure storage, not from the socket."
