        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/credential-leakage-via-url-query-string-handshake-header-sec-websocket-protocol",
          "ruleIndex": 125,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Credential leakage via URL query string / handshake header / Sec-WebSocket-Protocol — No issue identified: All credential-attach sites (gateway auth frame, chat/TTS Authorization headers, WS handshake)\n\nNo credential is ever placed in a URL or header by the transport layer: the gateway token is sent only as the `token` field of the `auth` JSON frame (gateway_client.dart:212-216), and the LLM/TTS clients use an `Authorization: Bearer` header (chat_datasource.dart:51, voice_output_service.dart:258, probe service :23/:70). Grep for query-string/token-parameter patterns and `Sec-WebSocket-Protocol` across `lib/` returns no credential-carrying usage; `IoGatewaySocketFactory.connect` (gateway_socket.dart:69-74) passes only caller-supplied headers and the app supplies none. Note dart:io itself would convert URL userinfo into a Basic auth header (websocket_impl.dart), but `isAcceptableGatewayUrl`/`normalizeGatewayUri` never require or add userinfo, so that path is not exercised by app-controlled input."
          },
