        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/path-traversal-arbitrary-file-write-via-an-auto-executing-tier-1-file-writing-tool",
          "ruleIndex": 126,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Path traversal / arbitrary file write via an auto-executing Tier-1 file-writing tool — No issue identified: export_document_pdf tool (doc_builder_skill.dart:33-71, registered tier1Auto)\n\n`export_document_pdf` (lib/data/datasources/skills/doc_builder_skill.dart:33-71) is registered at `securityTier: SecurityTier.tier1Auto` (:62) and wired manually at injection.config.dart:391-392, so it auto-executes with no gate — it belongs to the Tier-1 misclassification family already filed as vuln-0005. However the path-traversal angle is ruled out by a named control: the output filename is built by `_slugify` (doc_builder_skill.dart:125-132) which lowercases and replaces every character outside `[a-z0-9]` with `_`, then strips leading/trailing underscores and caps at 60 chars, before joining to `<documents dir>/documents/doc_<slug>_<stamp>.pdf` (:91-97). Model-controlled `title` and `outputFileName` therefore cannot inject `/`, `..`, or a separator into the path, and the write target is confined to the app documents directory via `getDocumentsDirectory()`. No traversal or arbitrary-write impact."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
